course: dictionary
lesson: 6373
title: Fish that skip on mud
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mudskipper is a small fish, and its name is a clue. It lives in mud and it skips. «Mudskippers are fish of mangrove swamps that skip across the mud on their fins.» So a mudskipper is a fish that moves across muddy ground, not just through water.
explain: Good readers use context to check their guess. The sentence says the fish has strong fins, and it can come out of the water. Ask yourself: does a fish that comes out of the water fit the clues? Yes, it does. Then check that your meaning still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Scientists find mudskippers interesting because they are between water and land. «Mudskippers are fish that spend lots of time out of the water, on mud.» They keep water in their gill chambers and breathe partly through their skin.
fact: A mudskipper is a small fish that lives on muddy shores and in mangrove swamps.
fact: Mudskippers can come out of the water, skipping and crawling on the mud with their strong front fins.
fact: «Mudskippers are fish that spend lots of time out of the water, on mud.»
fact: Mudskippers live in warm places such as Africa, Asia and northern Australia.
fact: Mudskippers help scientists think about how fish might once have moved onto land.
exercise: «Mudskippers are fish of mangrove swamps that skip across the mud on their fins.» What is a mudskipper? | A crab that lives in the deep sea | A bird that lives in swamps | A tall tree with breathing roots | *A small fish that can come out of the water and skip across mud
exercise: «Mudskippers are fish of mangrove swamps that skip across the mud on their fins.» Which body part helps a mudskipper skip across mud? | *Fins | Tail | Eyes | Ears
exercise: Where do mudskippers live? | *On muddy shores and in mangrove swamps | Deep in the ocean | In the middle of a desert | On the Arctic ice
test: «Males jump high to show off and defend their patch of mud.» Why do male mudskippers jump high? | To hide from the sun | *To show off and defend their patch of mud | To catch a bus | To go to sleep
test: Mudskippers are fish that spend lots of time out of the water. What kind of animal is a mudskipper? | A bird | A mammal | *A fish | A plant
exam: Read «fish like mudskippers even walk out onto the mud.» What does this tell you about mudskippers? | *They can move onto land for a while | They never leave the sea | They fly over the mud | They dig holes in the sand
